        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change introduces a verbatim duplication of a non-trivial business rule across two layers.\n\n**Finding: `fiscalYearStart(LocalDate)` is now duplicated in `ClinicServiceImpl` and `OwnerMapper`.**\n\nBefore this change the \"fiscal year starts 1 July\" rule lived in exactly one place \u2014 `OwnerMapper.fiscalYearStart`. The diff adds an identical private static copy to `ClinicServiceImpl`:\n\n```java\nprivate static int fiscalYearStart(LocalDate date) {\n    return date.getMonthValue() >= 7 ? date.getYear() : date.getYear() - 1;\n}\n```\n\nThis is the same rule the mapper already encodes (`OwnerMapper.fiscalYearStart`, still retained for the `formatFiscalYear` fallback). The FY boundary is a real business rule; having two authoritative copies means a future change to the fiscal-year start has to be made in two units that don't know about each other. This belongs in one place \u2014 the codebase already has a `util` package (`LocalityResolver`, `LuhnCheckDigit`, `Sha256Hex`) that is the natural home for a small `FiscalYear` helper both the service (which now encodes FY into the memberId) and the mapper (which reads/falls back to it) can call.\n\n**Secondary note (optional):** the memberId layout is now split knowledge \u2014 the service *builds* `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` while the mapper *parses* it via `memberIdBody`/`memberIdRegion`/`memberIdFiscalYear` using the magic length `11` (2+8+1) and offset arithmetic. The field widths are an invariant shared by both units but asserted independently in each. This follows the pre-existing pattern of parsing the identifier in the mapper (the old code split `customerCode` on `'-'`), so it is not strictly required to change; but if the FY helper is extracted, consider whether the segment offsets/widths also warrant a single shared definition so the two sides can't drift. The primary, actionable item is the `fiscalYearStart` duplication above."
      }
